# Europe/London — IANA tzdb 2026b slice (pinned fixture)
#
# PROVENANCE & TRANSFORM
# ----------------------
# Derived mechanically from /usr/share/zoneinfo/tzdata.zi (IANA tzdb 2026b, the installed
# single-file zishrink form) by expanding ONLY the leading record keywords:
#     R -> Rule      Z -> Zone      L -> Link
# Nothing else is changed. Month/weekday/year tokens are left in their zic-style abbreviated
# form (e.g. `O`, `Ap`, `lastSu`, `o`, `ma`) because zic-rs accepts unambiguous-prefix names
# exactly as reference `zic` does (see src/source/names.rs). zishrink record-key shorthand is
# a separate parser-breadth item (zic-rs's record dispatch is exact-match), NOT a London
# semantic blocker — documented in docs/unsupported-syntax.md.
#
# FAITHFULNESS PROOF
# ------------------
# Reference `zic` (tzcode 2026b) compiles this canonical slice to a TZif file that is
# BYTE-IDENTICAL to the one it produces from the unmodified abbreviated extract (verified with
# `cmp`). So the only-record-keys transform preserves semantics exactly.
#
# ORACLE STATUS
# -------------
# zic-rs output matches reference `zic` under the `zdump` behaviour oracle over 1830..2045
# (see docs/compatibility.md). This is behaviour (semantic) parity, the project's bar; the
# explicit-transition representation may differ (slim/fat) — byte-parity is not claimed here.
